IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc22-trial`

-- ccc22-tests-trial.l4 -- tests for ccc22-trial.l4 (sections 645 to 654). Expected values are written from the text, beside the assertion. Arguments are in the order of each function's GIVEN lines.

§ `Sections 645 and 646`

-- 645(1): args: the court has adjourned the trial.
#ASSERT `s 645(1) the trial must proceed continuously` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 645(1) the trial must proceed continuously` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "subject to adjournment by the court"
-- 645(2): args: the adjournment is from time to time in the same sittings.
#ASSERT `s 645(2) a judge may adjourn the trial` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 645(2) a judge may adjourn the trial` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an adjournment not within the stated limit is not decided here
-- 645(3): args: the adjournment is for the purpose of subsection (2).
#ASSERT `s 645(3) a formal adjournment of the trial or an entry of it is required` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "no formal adjournment of trial or entry thereof is required"
#ASSERT `s 645(3) a formal adjournment of the trial or an entry of it is required` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 645(3.1): args: the judge is deciding whether to adjourn, information related to the victim's interests is readily available.
#ASSERT `s 645(3.1) the judge must consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 645(3.1) the judge must consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the duty is "if information ... is readily available"
#ASSERT `s 645(3.1) the judge must consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a decision whether to adjourn
#ASSERT `s 645(3.1) the judge must consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 645(4): args: the case is tried without a jury.
#ASSERT `s 645(4) a judge may reserve final decision on any question raised at the trial, or any matter raised further to a pre-hearing conference` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 645(4) a judge may reserve final decision on any question raised at the trial, or any matter raised further to a pre-hearing conference` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a case tried with a jury is outside the stated limit
-- 645(4) deemed: args: the decision was reserved under subsection (4), the decision has been given.
#ASSERT `s 645(4) the decision is deemed to have been given at the trial` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 645(4) the decision is deemed to have been given at the trial` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "when given": not yet given
#ASSERT `s 645(4) the decision is deemed to have been given at the trial` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not reserved under the subsection
#ASSERT `s 645(4) the decision is deemed to have been given at the trial` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 645(5): args: tried with a jury, no juror yet called under 631(3) or (3.1), a matter ordinarily dealt with in the absence of the jury.
#ASSERT `s 645(5) the judge has jurisdiction to deal with the matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 645(5) the judge has jurisdiction to deal with the matter` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 645(5) the judge has jurisdiction to deal with the matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a juror has already been called
#ASSERT `s 645(5) the judge has jurisdiction to deal with the matter` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 646: args: trial for an indictable offence, the provision is one of Part XVIII on taking evidence at preliminary inquiries, the provision.
#ASSERT `s 646 the provision of Part XVIII applies to the taking of the evidence and the addresses` TRUE TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 540, "(6)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 646 the provision of Part XVIII applies to the taking of the evidence and the addresses` TRUE TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 540, "(7)") EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than subsections 540(7) to (9)": the first
#ASSERT `s 646 the provision of Part XVIII applies to the taking of the evidence and the addresses` TRUE TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 540, "(8)") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 646 the provision of Part XVIII applies to the taking of the evidence and the addresses` TRUE TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 540, "(9)") EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the last
#ASSERT `s 646 the provision of Part XVIII applies to the taking of the evidence and the addresses` TRUE TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 540, "(10)") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- just outside the excluded range
#ASSERT `s 646 the provision of Part XVIII applies to the taking of the evidence and the addresses` TRUE TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 541, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 646 the provision of Part XVIII applies to the taking of the evidence and the addresses` FALSE TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 541, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a trial for an indictable offence
#ASSERT `s 646 the provision of Part XVIII applies to the taking of the evidence and the addresses` TRUE FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 541, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a provision on taking evidence at preliminary inquiries

§ `Sections 647 and 648`

-- 647(1): args: the jury has retired to consider its verdict.
#ASSERT `s 647(1) the judge may permit the members of the jury to separate` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 647(1) the judge may permit the members of the jury to separate` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 647(1) the judge may permit the members of the jury to separate` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; a period the text fixes in its own words (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05), so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE, listed in the fork register as [F:may-where] with the other reading NOTHING; "at any time before the jury retires to consider its verdict"
-- 647(2): args: permission to separate cannot be given or is not given.
#ASSERT `s 647(2) the jury must be kept under the charge of an officer of the court as the judge directs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 647(2) the jury must be kept under the charge of an officer of the court as the judge directs` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- permission was given: the duty does not arise
-- 647(2) prevent: args: the juror would communicate with the officer or another member of the jury, the judge has given leave.
#ASSERT `s 647(2) the officer must prevent the juror from communicating` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 647(2) the officer must prevent the juror from communicating` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- communication with the officer or another juror is outside the duty
#ASSERT `s 647(2) the officer must prevent the juror from communicating` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "without leave of the judge"
#ASSERT `s 647(2) the officer must prevent the juror from communicating` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 647(3): args: the failure is a failure to comply with subsection 647(2).
#ASSERT `s 647(3) the failure to comply affects the validity of the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not affect the validity of the proceedings"
#ASSERT `s 647(3) the failure to comply affects the validity of the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 647(4): args: the failure is discovered before the verdict, the judge considers it might lead to a miscarriage of justice, the course.
#ASSERT `s 647(4) the judge may discharge the jury and take the course` TRUE TRUE `s 647(4)(a) direct that the accused be tried with a new jury during the same session or sittings of the court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 647(4) the judge may discharge the jury and take the course` TRUE TRUE `s 647(4)(b) postpone the trial on such terms as justice may require` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 647(4) the judge may discharge the jury and take the course` TRUE TRUE `s 647(4) some other course` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 647(4) the judge may discharge the jury and take the course` FALSE TRUE `s 647(4)(a) direct that the accused be tried with a new jury during the same session or sittings of the court` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Where ... discovered before the verdict" fails (a "where" gate, ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 647(4) the judge may discharge the jury and take the course` TRUE FALSE `s 647(4)(a) direct that the accused be tried with a new jury during the same session or sittings of the court` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the "if he considers" gate fails (a failed "if" on a grant: NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 647(4) the judge may discharge the jury and take the course` FALSE FALSE `s 647(4)(a) direct that the accused be tried with a new jury during the same session or sittings of the court` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the "where" gate is read first
-- 647(5): args: the jurors are sworn, the jurors are together, the jurors have given their verdict.
#ASSERT `s 647(5) the judge must direct the sheriff to provide the jurors with suitable and sufficient refreshment, food and lodging` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 647(5) the judge must direct the sheriff to provide the jurors with suitable and sufficient refreshment, food and lodging` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "while they are together"
#ASSERT `s 647(5) the judge must direct the sheriff to provide the jurors with suitable and sufficient refreshment, food and lodging` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "until they have given their verdict"
#ASSERT `s 647(5) the judge must direct the sheriff to provide the jurors with suitable and sufficient refreshment, food and lodging` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 647(5) the judge must direct the sheriff to provide the jurors with suitable and sufficient refreshment, food and lodging` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "the jurors who are sworn"
-- 648(1): args: permission to separate has been given, the information regards a portion of the trial at which the jury is not present, the jury has retired.
#ASSERT `s 648(1) the section bars publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the information` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 648(1) the section bars publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the information` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after the jury retires the period has ended
#ASSERT `s 648(1) the section bars publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the information` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before permission to separate is given
#ASSERT `s 648(1) the section bars publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the information` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- information about a portion at which the jury was present
#ASSERT `s 648(1) the section bars publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the information` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 648(2): args: the person fails to comply with subsection 648(1).
#ASSERT `s 648(2) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 648(2) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 648(2): the class and the punishment the subsection states (a summary conviction offence; no maximum stated).
#ASSERT `s 648(2) the class of offence` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT (`s 648(2) the punishment the subsection states`)'s `mode` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
#ASSERT (`s 648(2) the punishment the subsection states`)'s `maximum imprisonment` EQUALS `no imprisonment is stated`
#ASSERT (`s 648(2) the punishment the subsection states`)'s `maximum fine` EQUALS `no fine is stated`
#ASSERT `s 648(3) what the text shows` EQUALS "[Repealed, 2005, c. 32, s. 21]"

§ `Section 649`

-- 649(1): args: the person is a member of a jury or a support-services person, the person discloses information relating to the jury's proceedings when it was absent, the information was subsequently disclosed in open court.
#ASSERT `s 649(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 649(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "that was not subsequently disclosed in open court": outside the limit
#ASSERT `s 649(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a juror or support person
#ASSERT `s 649(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no disclosure
-- 649(1) as a rule: a juror who discloses is in breach; a juror who does not has done nothing wrong. expected: BREACHED
#TRACE `s 649(1) a juror shall not disclose information relating to the proceedings of the jury` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a juror` DOES `s 649(1) disclose information relating to the proceedings of the jury when it was absent from the courtroom` AT 5
-- expected: BREACHED ("the juror disclosed information relating to the proceedings of the jury when it was absent from the courtroom")
#TRACE `s 649(1) a juror shall not disclose information relating to the proceedings of the jury` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)
-- expected: the prohibition is still standing at 10 (residual obligation: PARTY a juror MUST NOT ...; the text states no time limit, so it is neither fulfilled nor breached)
-- 649(2): args: the purpose, the answer of section 649(3) for the health care professional.
#ASSERT `s 649(2) subsection (1) applies to the disclosure` `s 649(2)(a) an investigation of an alleged offence under subsection 139(2) in relation to a juror` NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not apply"
#ASSERT `s 649(2) subsection (1) applies to the disclosure` `s 649(2)(b) giving evidence in criminal proceedings in relation to such an offence` NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 649(2) subsection (1) applies to the disclosure` `s 649(2)(c) any medical or psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling that the person receives from a health care professional after the completion of the trial in relation to health issues arising out of or related to the person’s service at the trial` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 649(2) subsection (1) applies to the disclosure` `s 649(2)(c) any medical or psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling that the person receives from a health care professional after the completion of the trial in relation to health issues arising out of or related to the person’s service at the trial` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- a professional section 649(3) does not accept
#ASSERT `s 649(2) subsection (1) applies to the disclosure` `s 649(2)(c) any medical or psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling that the person receives from a health care professional after the completion of the trial in relation to health issues arising out of or related to the person’s service at the trial` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 649(2) subsection (1) applies to the disclosure` `s 649(2) some other purpose` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- a purpose outside the three listed
-- 649(3): args: the professional is entitled under the laws of a province.
#ASSERT `s 649(3) the health care professional is one for the purpose of paragraph (2)(c)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 649(3) the health care professional is one for the purpose of paragraph (2)(c)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "must be entitled to do so under the laws of a province"

§ `Sections 650 to 650.2`

-- 650(1): args: the accused is an organization (section 2 term, an input).
#ASSERT `s 650(1) the section requires the accused to be present in court during the whole of their trial` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650(1) the section requires the accused to be present in court during the whole of their trial` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than an organization"
#ASSERT `s 650(1) the section requires the accused to be present in court during the whole of their trial` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the accused is an organization is for the section 2 definition
-- 650(1) means: args: present in person, appears by audio or video conference authorized under sections 715.231 to 715.241.
#ASSERT `s 650(1) the accused’s presence meets the requirement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650(1) the accused’s presence meets the requirement` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650(1) the accused’s presence meets the requirement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650(1) the accused’s presence meets the requirement` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 650(1.1): args: the prosecutor consents, the accused consents, the part is one in which the evidence of a witness is taken.
#ASSERT `s 650(1.1) the court may allow the accused to appear by counsel for the part of the trial` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650(1.1) the court may allow the accused to appear by counsel for the part of the trial` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than a part in which the evidence of a witness is taken"
#ASSERT `s 650(1.1) the court may allow the accused to appear by counsel for the part of the trial` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no consent of the prosecutor
#ASSERT `s 650(1.1) the court may allow the accused to appear by counsel for the part of the trial` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no consent of the accused
#ASSERT `s 650(1.1) the court may allow the accused to appear by counsel for the part of the trial` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 650(1.2) what the text shows` EQUALS "[Repealed, 2022, c. 17, s. 39]"
-- 650(2): args: the course, the accused misconducts themself by interrupting, the court is satisfied about the adverse effect on the mental condition.
#ASSERT `s 650(2) the court may take the course` `s 650(2)(a) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court, where they misconduct themself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in their presence would not be feasible` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650(2) the court may take the course` `s 650(2)(a) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court, where they misconduct themself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in their presence would not be feasible` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 650(2) the court may take the course` `s 650(2)(b) permit the accused to be out of court during the whole or any part of the trial on such conditions as the court considers proper` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- no gate
#ASSERT `s 650(2) the court may take the course` `s 650(2)(c) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court during the trial of an issue as to whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650(2) the court may take the course` `s 650(2)(c) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court during the trial of an issue as to whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 650(2) the court may take the course` `s 650(2) some other course` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is not closed
-- 650(3): args: the case for the prosecution has closed.
#ASSERT `s 650(3) the accused is entitled to make full answer and defence personally or by counsel` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650(3) the accused is entitled to make full answer and defence personally or by counsel` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the stated period: "after the close of the case for the prosecution"
-- 650.01(1): args: the accused files a designation with the court.
#ASSERT `s 650.01(1) the accused may appoint counsel to represent the accused for any proceedings under this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(1) the accused may appoint counsel to represent the accused for any proceedings under this Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "by filing a designation": other ways are not decided here
-- 650.01(2): args: name, address, signed by the accused, signed by the designated counsel.
#ASSERT `s 650.01(2) the designation has the contents subsection (2) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(2) the designation has the contents subsection (2) requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(2) the designation has the contents subsection (2) requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(2) the designation has the contents subsection (2) requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(2) the designation has the contents subsection (2) requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 650.01(3)(a): args: a designation is filed, the part of the proceedings.
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(a) the accused may appear by the designated counsel without being present for the part` TRUE `s 650.01(3)(a) some other part of the proceedings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(a) the accused may appear by the designated counsel without being present for the part` TRUE `s 650.01(3)(a)(i) a part during which oral evidence of a witness is taken` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than (i)"
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(a) the accused may appear by the designated counsel without being present for the part` TRUE `s 650.01(3)(a)(ii) a part during which jurors are being selected` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(a) the accused may appear by the designated counsel without being present for the part` TRUE `s 650.01(3)(a)(iii) an application for a writ of habeas corpus` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(a) the accused may appear by the designated counsel without being present for the part` FALSE `s 650.01(3)(a) some other part of the proceedings` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "If a designation is filed" fails
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(a) the accused may appear by the designated counsel without being present for the part` FALSE `s 650.01(3)(a)(i) a part during which oral evidence of a witness is taken` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 650.01(3)(b): args: a designation is filed, the court orders otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(b) an appearance by the designated counsel is equivalent to the accused’s being present` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(b) an appearance by the designated counsel is equivalent to the accused’s being present` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the court orders otherwise"
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(b) an appearance by the designated counsel is equivalent to the accused’s being present` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 650.01(3)(c): args: a designation is filed, the accused is present, the court orders otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(c) a plea of guilty may be made and a sentence may be pronounced` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(c) a plea of guilty may be made and a sentence may be pronounced` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "unless the court orders otherwise"
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(c) a plea of guilty may be made and a sentence may be pronounced` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "only if the accused is present"
#ASSERT `s 650.01(3)(c) a plea of guilty may be made and a sentence may be pronounced` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 650.01(4): args: the court orders the accused to be present otherwise than by designated counsel, the step.
#ASSERT `s 650.01(4) the court may take the step to compel the presence of the accused` TRUE `s 650.01(4)(a) issue a summons to compel the presence of the accused and order that it be served by leaving a copy at the address contained in the designation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(4) the court may take the step to compel the presence of the accused` TRUE `s 650.01(4)(b) issue a warrant to compel the presence of the accused` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650.01(4) the court may take the step to compel the presence of the accused` TRUE `s 650.01(4) some other step` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 650.01(4) the court may take the step to compel the presence of the accused` FALSE `s 650.01(4)(a) issue a summons to compel the presence of the accused and order that it be served by leaving a copy at the address contained in the designation` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the "if" gate fails (a grant: NOTHING)
-- 650.02: args: the person is the prosecutor or the designated counsel, the technological means is satisfactory to the court.
#ASSERT `s 650.02 the prosecutor or the designated counsel may appear before the court by audioconference or videoconference` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650.02 the prosecutor or the designated counsel may appear before the court by audioconference or videoconference` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 650.02 the prosecutor or the designated counsel may appear before the court by audioconference or videoconference` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the "if" gate fails (a grant: NOTHING)
-- 650.1: args: a jury trial, the charge to the jury has been given.
#ASSERT `s 650.1 the judge may confer with the accused or counsel for the accused and the prosecutor about the matters to be explained to the jury and the instructions` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 650.1 the judge may confer with the accused or counsel for the accused and the prosecutor about the matters to be explained to the jury and the instructions` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 650.1 the judge may confer with the accused or counsel for the accused and the prosecutor about the matters to be explained to the jury and the instructions` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; a period the text fixes in its own words (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05), so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE, listed in the fork register as [F:may-where] with the other reading NOTHING; "before the charge to the jury"
#ASSERT `s 650.1 the judge may confer with the accused or counsel for the accused and the prosecutor about the matters to be explained to the jury and the instructions` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a jury trial

§ `Section 651`

-- 651(1) declare: args: the accused is defended by counsel, the case for the prosecution has ended.
#ASSERT `s 651(1) counsel must declare whether or not they intend to adduce evidence on behalf of the accused` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 651(1) counsel must declare whether or not they intend to adduce evidence on behalf of the accused` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the duty is "where ... defended by counsel"
#ASSERT `s 651(1) counsel must declare whether or not they intend to adduce evidence on behalf of the accused` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the end of the case for the prosecution
-- 651(1) as a rule: counsel who declares by time 10 has fulfilled the duty; one who does nothing by 11 is in breach.
#TRACE (`s 651(1) counsel must declare at the end of the case for the prosecution whether or not they intend to adduce evidence` 10) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `counsel for the accused` DOES `s 651(1) declare whether or not counsel intends to adduce evidence on behalf of the accused` AT 5
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE (`s 651(1) counsel must declare at the end of the case for the prosecution whether or not they intend to adduce evidence` 10) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 11)
-- expected: BREACHED ("counsel for the accused did not declare, at the end of the case for the prosecution, whether or not counsel intends to adduce evidence")
-- 651(1) prosecutor: args: the accused is defended by counsel, counsel announces an intention to adduce evidence.
#ASSERT `s 651(1) the prosecutor may address the jury by way of summing up` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 651(1) the prosecutor may address the jury by way of summing up` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "if he does not announce his intention": the "if" gate fails (a grant: NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 651(1) the prosecutor may address the jury by way of summing up` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 651(2): args: the person is counsel for the accused or the accused not defended, the step, the opening has concluded, all the evidence is concluded.
#ASSERT `s 651(2) counsel for the accused, or the accused where not defended by counsel, is entitled to take the step` TRUE `s 651(2) open the case for the defence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 651(2) counsel for the accused, or the accused where not defended by counsel, is entitled to take the step` TRUE `s 651(2) examine such witnesses as they think fit, after the conclusion of the opening` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 651(2) counsel for the accused, or the accused where not defended by counsel, is entitled to take the step` TRUE `s 651(2) examine such witnesses as they think fit, after the conclusion of the opening` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "after the conclusion of that opening"
#ASSERT `s 651(2) counsel for the accused, or the accused where not defended by counsel, is entitled to take the step` TRUE `s 651(2) sum up the evidence, when all the evidence is concluded` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 651(2) counsel for the accused, or the accused where not defended by counsel, is entitled to take the step` TRUE `s 651(2) sum up the evidence, when all the evidence is concluded` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "when all the evidence is concluded"
#ASSERT `s 651(2) counsel for the accused, or the accused where not defended by counsel, is entitled to take the step` FALSE `s 651(2) open the case for the defence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not counsel for the accused, or an accused not defended by counsel
#ASSERT `s 651(2) counsel for the accused, or the accused where not defended by counsel, is entitled to take the step` TRUE `s 651(2) some other step` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is not closed
-- 651(3): args: no witnesses are examined for the accused.
#ASSERT `s 651(3) who is entitled to address the jury last` TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 651(3) the accused or their counsel`
#ASSERT `s 651(3) who is entitled to address the jury last` FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 651(3) counsel for the prosecution`
-- 651(4): args: two or more accused are tried jointly, witnesses are examined for any of them.
#ASSERT `s 651(4) all the accused or their respective counsel must address the jury before it is addressed by the prosecutor` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 651(4) all the accused or their respective counsel must address the jury before it is addressed by the prosecutor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no witness examined for any of them
#ASSERT `s 651(4) all the accused or their respective counsel must address the jury before it is addressed by the prosecutor` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one accused only

§ `Sections 652 to 654`

-- 652(1) view: args: it appears to be in the interests of justice, the jury has been sworn, the jury has given its verdict.
#ASSERT `s 652(1) the judge may direct the jury to have a view of any place, thing or person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 652(1) the judge may direct the jury to have a view of any place, thing or person` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 652(1) the judge may direct the jury to have a view of any place, thing or person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 652(1) the judge may direct the jury to have a view of any place, thing or person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING`; a period the text fixes in its own words (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05), so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE, listed in the fork register as [F:may-where] with the other reading NOTHING; before the jury is sworn
#ASSERT `s 652(1) the judge may direct the jury to have a view of any place, thing or person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 652(1) the judge may direct the jury to have a view of any place, thing or person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING`; a period the text fixes in its own words (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05), so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE, listed in the fork register as [F:may-where] with the other reading NOTHING; after the verdict
#ASSERT `s 652(1) the judge may direct the jury to have a view of any place, thing or person` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the "where" gate is read first
-- 652(1) directions: args: the judge directs the jury to have a view.
#ASSERT `s 652(1) the judge must give directions respecting the manner in which, and the persons by whom, the place, thing or person shall be shown to the jury` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 652(1) the judge must give directions respecting the manner in which, and the persons by whom, the place, thing or person shall be shown to the jury` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 652(2): args: a view is ordered, the judge considers directions necessary.
#ASSERT `s 652(2) the judge must give the directions` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 652(2) the judge must give the directions` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the duty is "where a view is ordered"
#ASSERT `s 652(2) the judge must give the directions` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "any directions that he considers necessary": none considered necessary
-- 652(2) failure: args: the failure is a failure to comply with directions given under subsection 652(2).
#ASSERT `s 652(2) the failure to comply with the directions affects the validity of the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not affect the validity of the proceedings"
#ASSERT `s 652(2) the failure to comply with the directions affects the validity of the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 652(3): args: a view is ordered under subsection (1).
#ASSERT `s 652(3) the accused and the judge must attend the view` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 652(3) the accused and the judge must attend the view` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 652.1(1): args: the charge to the jury has been given.
#ASSERT `s 652.1(1) the jury must retire to try the issues of the indictment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 652.1(1) the jury must retire to try the issues of the indictment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "After the charge to the jury"
-- 652.1(2): args: the number of jurors remaining. 12 or fewer: no card; 13: one card; 14: two cards.
#ASSERT `s 652.1(2) the number of cards the judge must draw to identify the 12 jurors who are to retire` 11 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 652.1(2) the number of cards the judge must draw to identify the 12 jurors who are to retire` 12 EQUALS JUST 0   -- "if there are more than 12 jurors remaining": 12 is not more than 12
#ASSERT `s 652.1(2) the number of cards the judge must draw to identify the 12 jurors who are to retire` 13 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 652.1(2) the number of cards the judge must draw to identify the 12 jurors who are to retire` 14 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `s 652.1(2) the number of cards the judge must draw to identify the 12 jurors who are to retire` 15 EQUALS NOTHING   -- subsection 631(2.2) allows 13 or 14 only; the text names no other number
-- 653(1): args: the judge is satisfied that the jury is unable to agree and further detention would be useless, the step.
#ASSERT `s 653(1) the judge may take the step` TRUE `s 653(1) discharge that jury and direct a new jury to be empanelled during the sittings of the court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 653(1) the judge may take the step` TRUE `s 653(1) adjourn the trial on such terms as justice may require` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 653(1) the judge may take the step` TRUE `s 653(1) some other step` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 653(1) the judge may take the step` FALSE `s 653(1) discharge that jury and direct a new jury to be empanelled during the sittings of the court` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "where" gate (ruling (b))
-- 653(2): args: the discretion was exercised under subsection (1).
#ASSERT `s 653(2) the exercise of the discretion is reviewable` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not reviewable"
#ASSERT `s 653(2) the exercise of the discretion is reviewable` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 653.1: args: there is a mistrial, the rulings relate to disclosure or admissibility of evidence or the Charter, the rulings are made (or could have been made) before the evidence on the merits, the court is satisfied that it would not be in the interests of justice.
#ASSERT `s 653.1 the rulings made during the trial are binding on the parties in any new trial` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 653.1 the rulings made during the trial are binding on the parties in any new trial` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a mistrial
#ASSERT `s 653.1 the rulings made during the trial are binding on the parties in any new trial` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the court is satisfied that it would not be in the interests of justice"
#ASSERT `s 653.1 the rulings made during the trial are binding on the parties in any new trial` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- rulings on some other subject
#ASSERT `s 653.1 the rulings made during the trial are binding on the parties in any new trial` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- rulings that could only be made after the merits evidence began
-- 654: args: the proceeding is the taking of the verdict or one incidental to it, the only ground is that it is done on Sunday or on a holiday.
#ASSERT `s 654 the taking of the verdict, or a proceeding incidental to it, is invalid` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not invalid by reason only that it is done on Sunday or on a holiday"
#ASSERT `s 654 the taking of the verdict, or a proceeding incidental to it, is invalid` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 654 the taking of the verdict, or a proceeding incidental to it, is invalid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- some other ground: not decided here
